---
import SiteFooter from "../components/SiteFooter.astro";
import SiteHeader from "../components/SiteHeader.astro";
import SiteLayout from "../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Privacy — Presently"
  description="How Presently handles photos, account information, and public story records."
>
  <SiteHeader />
  <main class="legal-page">
    <article class="shell legal-content">
      <p class="legal-date">Last Updated July 27, 2026</p>
      <h1>Privacy</h1>
      <p class="legal-intro">
        Presently is built to help you share a photo without building another
        attention-driven feed. The app keeps your account credentials and photo
        workflow on your device.
      </p>

      <h2>Photos You Choose to Share</h2>
      <p>
        A photo remains on your device while it is being prepared. When you
        post, Presently uploads that photo directly to your AT Protocol Personal
        Data Server and creates a public Flashes-compatible story record in your
        repository.
      </p>

      <h2>Public Stories and Expiration</h2>
      <p>
        Story records are public repository data. Flashes-compatible apps stop
        displaying a story after its 24-hour window, but public network data may
        have been indexed, cached, or replicated elsewhere. Expiration is not a
        promise that every copy is physically deleted.
      </p>

      <h2>Your Account</h2>
      <p>
        Sign-in happens with your account provider. Presently stores the session
        and cryptographic keys in your device’s secure storage. The Presently
        metadata service does not receive your password, access tokens, refresh
        tokens, private keys, or captured photos.
      </p>

      <h2>Local Storage and Your Photo Library</h2>
      <p>
        Pending and failed drafts may remain on your device so a post can be
        retried safely. Saving a separate copy to your photo library follows the
        preference you choose in the app.
      </p>

      <h2>Diagnostics</h2>
      <p>
        Presently does not use advertising trackers. If privacy-safe diagnostics
        are added for beta testing, they will measure app outcomes such as
        capture or publish success and will never contain photos, tokens, or
        private keys.
      </p>

      <h2>Questions</h2>
      <p>
        Visit <a href="/support/">Support</a> for the current way to report a
        privacy concern or request help.
      </p>
    </article>
  </main>
  <SiteFooter />
</SiteLayout>
